# rsync filter for publishing a run (merged by grib_copy_to_server.sh and
# run.sh --local). Only the forecast products below are copied, and with
# --delete only they are removed from the destination when the new run did
# not produce them, so a failed hour can't leave the previous run's frame
# behind under the same name. Everything else in the destination is
# excluded and therefore untouched: metadata.json (copied separately, last)
# and any .gz siblings the web app generates there.
# Tide predictions are astronomical, so a run whose tide fetch failed keeps
# the previous spot_tides file rather than deleting it (P: never delete).
P spot_tides.json.gz
+ *.geojson
+ *.geojson.gz
+ *.png
+ tides.json
+ spot_forecasts.json.gz
+ spot_tides.json.gz
- *
